    "conclusion": "1. 1.6 cm nodular opacity in the left upper lung zone. Recommend CT chest for further characterization.\n2. Hyperinflation, which can be seen with COPD.\n3. No acute cardiopulmonary process.",
    "presentedForm": [
      {
        "contentType": "text/plain",
        "text": "EXAM:\nXR CHEST, 2 VIEWS (PA AND LATERAL)\n\nCLINICAL INDICATION:\nPreoperative evaluation before elective right total knee arthroplasty.\n\nTECHNIQUE:\nPA and lateral views of the chest.\n\nCOMPARISON:\nNone available.\n\nFINDINGS:\nLungs: The lungs are hyperinflated with flattening of the hemidiaphragms. There is a 1.6 cm rounded nodular opacity projecting over the left upper lung zone, best seen on the frontal view. No consolidation, pleural effusion, or pneumothorax.\nHeart and mediastinum: Heart size is within normal limits. Calcification of the aortic knob. Mediastinal contours are otherwise normal.\nBones: Degenerative changes of the thoracic spine. No acute osseous abnormality.\n\nIMPRESSION:\n1. 1.6 cm nodular opacity in the left upper lung zone. Recommend CT chest for further characterization.\n2. Hyperinflation, which can be seen with COPD.\n3. No acute cardiopulmonary process."
      }
    ]
  },
